py Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe prove recent conjectures of Chern concerning nonnegativity of a certain q-series related to parity bias in integer partitions.\n\n  * On $k$-measures and Durfee squares of partitions\n\nDamanvir Singh Binner\n\nJun 07 2022 math.CO arXiv:2206.02778v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2206.02778, author = {Damanvir Singh Binner}, title = {{O}n $k$-measures and {D}urfee squares of partitions}, year = {2022}, eprint = {2206.02778}, note = {arXiv:2206.02778v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nRecently, Andrews, Bhattacharjee and Dastidar introduced the concept of $k$-measure of an integer partition, and proved a surprising identity that the number of partitions of $n$ which have $2$-measure $m$ is equal to the number of partitions of $n$ with a Durfee square of side $m$. The authors asked for a bijective proof of this result and also suggested a further exploration of the properties of the number of partitions of $n$ which have $k$-measure $m$ for $k \\geq 3$. In this note, we complete these tasks. That is, we obtain a short combinatorial proof of the result of Andrews, Bhattacharjee and Dastidar, and using this proof, we easily generalize this result for $k$-measures.\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2204.07218, author = {Damanvir Singh Binner}, title = {{N}umber of partitions of n with a given parity of the smallest part}, year = {2022}, eprint = {2204.07218}, note = {arXiv:2204.07218v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe obtain a combinatorial proof of a surprising weighted partition equality of Berkovich and Uncu. Our proof naturally leads to a formula for the number of partitions with a given parity of the smallest part, in terms of S(i), the number of partitions of i into distinct parts with even rank minus the number with odd rank, for which there is an almost closed formula by Andrews, Dyson and Hickerson. This method of calculating the number of partitions of n with a given parity of the smallest part is practical and efficient.\n\n  * Proofs of Chappelon and Alfonsı́n Conjectures On Square Frobenius Numbers and its Relationship to Simultaneous Pell's Equations\n\nDamanvir Singh Binner\n\nJan 03 2022 math.NT arXiv:2112.15474v1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nREFERENCES\n\n[1] G. E. Andrews. On a partition prob (https://mat.univie.ac.at/~schlosse/pdf/ResClBi.pdf)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; *The theory of partitions*. ... On conjectures of Chern concerning parity bias in partitions. *arXiv:2209.05949*.\nREFERENCES\n\n[1] G. E. Andrews. On a partition problem of H. L. Alder. *Pacific J. Math.*, 36:279–284, 1971.  \n[2] G. E. Andrews. *The theory of partitions*. Encyclopedia of Mathematics and its Applications, Vol. 2. Addison-Wesley Publishing Co., Reading, Mass.-London-Amsterdam, 1976.  \n[3] G. E. Andrews and B. C. Berndt. *Ramanujan’s lost notebook. Part III*. Springer, New York, 2012.  \n[4] K. Banerjee, S. Bhattacharjee, M. G. Dastidar, P. Jyoti Mahanta, and Manjil P. Saikia. Parity biases in partitions and restricted partitions. *European J. Combin.*, 103:Paper No. 103522, 19, 2022.  \n[5] D. S. Binner. On conjectures of Chern concerning parity bias in partitions. *arXiv:2209.05949*.  \n[6] R. Brenti. Determinants of super-Schur functions, lattice paths, and dotted plane partitions. *Adv. Math.*, 98(1): 27–64, 1993.  \n[7] S. Chern. Further results on biases in integer partitions. *Bull. Korean Math. Soc.*, 59(1):111–117, 2022.  \n[8] S. Corteel and J. Lovejoy. Overpartitions. *Trans. Amer. Math. Soc.*, 356(4): 1623–1635, 2004.  \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDatabase | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/database?tag=binomial-edge-ideals)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;   * ## Jayanthan–Raghavan conjecture on linear type binomial edge ideals\n\n# 31 problems\n\n[Button: Trending][Button: Newest][Button: